      "sha256": "7a792746cd5bf122937636e53197ba6a5b09127dee51b96e6f180351bdfbb6ab",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "This figure illustrates the process of generalizing a parameter XPath from the unique XPath string for original value \"Apple\" to a generalized XPath formula to match all values for the \"fruit\" parameter. The first line of the figure is the unique XPath \"html > ... > .section[1] > .fruit[1] > div[1] > span[2]\", which matches the text \"Apple\" only. An arrow is then drawn to the next line, \"html > ... > .section[1] > .fruit[1] > div[index] > span[2]\", where \"div[1]\" is generalized to \"div[index]\", which results in this XPath now matching the text \"Apple\", \"Banana\", and \"Pineapple\". Finally, an arrow is drawn from this second line to the third/last line, \"html > ... > .section[1] > .fruit[1] > div[index] > span.description\", where \"span[2]\" is generalized to \"span.description\", resulting in the final generalized XPath formula which matches \"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Pineapple\", and now \"Fig\" too."
    }
